According to Hong Kong's "Oriental Daily" reported on August 12, at present, there are three major problems in mainland diamond sales, including the purity of fake diamonds to push up the price, the weight of virtual diamonds, and the lack of after-sales protection.
Antwerp is one of the world's largest diamond trading centers, the local craftsmen's diamond cutting technology is full of names, and the diamonds sold have been rigorously identified and welcomed by mainland ladies.
"A small cloth bag, held in the palm of your hand, a small number of light floats, worth nearly one million yuan," an aunt surnamed Liu, who participated in the purchase of diamonds, described her experience in Antwerp in June this year to the mainland media.
She pointed out that she hid the diamond in her underwear, went to the toilet for a few days, took a bath, and was very nervous to walk and sleep.
She said that the diamonds bought in Antwerp were purchased for about 55,000 yuan per carat, and the retail price of diamonds of the same quality in Xiamen was about 111,000 yuan.
A few days ago, she added 20% to the purchase price, sold all the diamonds she purchased, and made more than 200,000 yuan at a time.
According to mainland customs regulations, the goods or necessities of non-passengers of diamonds in the itinerary belong to the category of goods, and they need to be declared at the time of entry and exit, otherwise they will be listed for smuggling, and the situation can be sentenced to prison in serious cases.
