China's Mars Project has arrived.
China's Mars exploration mission is required to circumnavigate, land and patrol once, and this form has never happened abroad.
China's Mars exploration and launch goal is to want a step around, landing, patrol, this mission is quite difficult.
Because it will take 26 months for Mars exploration to encounter a window of time, experts are working closely to develop engineering plans to launch China's first Mars probe at this window in 2020.
According to Xu Dazhe, although China's aircraft has entered deep space, but the completion of the Mars exploration mission is still indispensable, the exploration of Mars means that China from a true sense into the era of deep space exploration.
“Every two or three years there is only one chance that Mars is closest to Earth, and the launch of a Mars probe at this point in time is the most energy-efficient for launch vehicles.”
“Taking into account the quality of the Mars probe, it will be up to China's Long March 5 launch vehicle to complete the launch mission.”
China's Mars exploration mission is to achieve a circumnavigation, landing, inspection, this form has never happened in foreign countries, foreign countries have planned to achieve an orbit and landing, but the landing failed.
There are many technical fields involved in the exploration of Mars, in particular, although the rover is a space probe, but compared with the general space probe, it also has distinctive characteristics.
That is to say, the Mars probe must have the ability to determine the route of travel and find the danger of obstacles.
Pang Zhihao, a researcher at the Fifth Academy of the China Aerospace Science and Technology Group, said that the reason why human beings are so popular for Mars exploration is that the exploration of Mars has important scientific and technological significance, even related to the future of mankind.
At present, Mars has become the most highly researched planet outside of Earth, and the history of humans using space probes to carry out Mars exploration has penetrated almost the entire history of human spaceflight.
As a result, humanity hopes to one day establish a residential base on Mars, and eventually migrate to Mars, turning it into a second home for humanity.
There are also plenty of signs that Mars is likely to be the same as the current Earth, only after billions of years of evolution to become a thin atmosphere, low temperatures, water depletion and so on.
Therefore, the exploration or manned landing on Mars for research can provide a plan to prevent Earth from becoming the second Mars that is difficult for humans to survive.
As of June 2016, there have been 114 lunar explorations and 43 explorations on Mars.
However, since the 1990s, humans have carried out a total of 18 Mars explorations, and only 14 lunar explorations.
There are currently five Mars orbiters and two Mars rovers at work, but only one lunar orbiter and one lunar lander are at work.
The world's space powers have all formulated exploration plans aimed at the Mars system, which shows that today's Mars exploration is hotter than lunar exploration.
On November 5, 2013, India launched its first Mars probe, Mangarian, becoming the first country in Asia to successfully explore Mars.
"Mangarian" is used to study the surface, atmosphere and mineral characteristics of Mars, and to explore whether there are signs of methane and life on Mars.
The most difficult part of this mission is that the probe has only one chance to slow down after entering the Martian atmosphere.
According to Sun Zezhou, chief designer of the Mars probe of the general department of the Fifth Academy of China Aerospace Science and Technology Corporation, the Mars exploration mission faces many technical challenges.
The atmospheric pressure of Mars is very low, only 1% of the atmospheric pressure on the earth's surface, which has a high degree of uncertainty.
Scientists do not yet have a thorough understanding of factors such as its changes and the characteristics of the storm.
Mars often forms dust storms similar to Earth's sand and dust weather in the summer, which will lead to a sharp decline in the sunlight energy received by the Mars rover, which must design a "sleeping" mode for the rover, allowing it to wait patiently for the dust storm to pass.
At the same time, the Martian atmosphere has a reduced effect on solar light, which brings problems to the energy supply of Mars exploration.
This requires that the probe's solar wing area is larger, and it needs to be constantly adjusted to focus on the direction of the sun.
In addition, the surface gravity of Mars is only 38% of that of Earth, but it is much more than the gravity on the surface of the moon, so the probe needs more power.
“The core and most difficult part of this Mars exploration mission is the process of the probe's pneumatic appearance and parachute deceleration after entering the Martian atmosphere, there is only one chance to ensure success.”
Sun Zezhou said that due to the distance between Earth and Mars, the whole process cannot be controlled by the ground in real time, so it must rely on the probe to complete it autonomously.
Since there aren’t that many propellants to offset that high speed, the deceleration depends on the action of the Martian atmosphere when landing on Mars, but it is difficult to simulate the Martian atmosphere on the ground.
Pang Zhihao said that in general, the way to explore Mars is similar to the way of exploring the moon, but also "circling, falling, patrolling, returning", and finally achieving the goal of manned landing on Mars.
Because Mars is much farther from Earth than the moon, exploring Mars requires overcoming a series of more complex technical difficulties.
According to Taiwanese media reports, Taiwan's "Administrative President" Lin Quan announced yesterday morning that the "Regulations on Impropriated Access to Property by Political Parties and Affiliated Organizations" will come into effect from today.
Zhan Qixian, vice chairman of the Kuomintang, said: "A 100-year-old Kuomintang, with social commitments and responsibilities, won't fail in this way."
Lin Quan stressed that if political parties, affiliated organizations or fiduciary managers, etc., violate the prohibitions stipulated in the regulations, the Committee will investigate and impose sanctions and penalties "in accordance with the law".
Lin Quan also announced that the candidates of the deputy chairman of the party property committee will be held by Hong Bacon, deputy director of Taiwan's "ICCAC."
He said that Gu Lixiong as the main chairman of the improper party production committee is not two candidates, borrowing Hong Bacon's past experience to investigate related major cases will serve as the basis for the committee's inventory of relevant improper party property cases.
Zhan Qixian believes that as long as there is party property today, no one will give you social donations, and if the party property system is confiscated, the Kuomintang can just ask for social support and sponsorship.
Zhan Qixian also stressed that even after improper party property regulations on the road, the Kuomintang party property has not been completely confiscated and confiscated, and the rest will still be donated according to the promise, so that the party's property is zero, and the party wants everything to start from scratch.
Original title: "Calliance doctor" Lan Yuefeng v. CCTV host Wang Zhi'an's first-instance of defamation infringement
Legal Evening News because CCTV host Wang Zhi'an published remarks on the "corridor doctor" incident on Sina Weibo, Lan Yuefeng sued Wang Zhi'an and Beijing Weizhong Chuangke Network Technology Co., Ltd. to the court.
Yesterday afternoon, the Haidian court issued a judgment on the case, the judgment found that Wang Zhi'an and micro-dream company did not constitute infringement, and rejected all Lan Yuefeng's claims.
At the beginning of 2014, CCTV reporter Wang Zhi'an's investigation found that although Lanyue Peak, who sat in the hospital corridor for more than 600 days, was portrayed by the media as a tragic hero suppressed by the system, there was a lot of false information about these reports.
On March 29, 2014, the "Doctor in the Corridor" program produced by the CCTV news investigation was broadcast.
There is no evidence to support all kinds of so-called excessive medical information reported to the media.
Wang Zhi'an is also in the real-name-certified micro-blog, describing "Lan Yuefeng's coming to this point is that his personality makes sense and has an obvious paranoid personality."
Lan Yuefeng asked Wang Zhi'an to delete Weibo, apologize to him and compensate 100,000 yuan for moral damage.
During the trial at that time, the two sides debated whether Wang Zhi'an had violated Lan Yuefeng's reputation rights.
