After the ceremony, the participating participants visited the Shandong Yuanshan Harvory and Entrepreneurship Memorial Museum and experienced the construction of barrier-free facilities.
Rivas Mayor Vilfredo López said at the teacher training site that the Nicaraguan government agencies are working together with the HKND Group to promote environmental management plans and carry out tree planting activities.
The HKND Group, as the developer of the canal project, has always followed the best international practices to build canals in accordance with international standards, so as to maximize the protection of Nicaragua’s ecological environment.”
Through the combination of theory and practice, college students lead primary and secondary school students to plant trees together to educate the next generation of Nicaragua on how to green the environment.
Francisco Reyes, a professor in the Department of Natural Resources and the Environment of the National Agricultural University of Nicaragua, took the whole team to participate in afforestation education projects.
We have reason to believe that the Transoceanic Grand Canal project, also led by the HKND Group, will bring more benefits to the people of Nicaragua and create more local employment opportunities.”
