"We must carry forward the talents we have learned from the country in Russia."
On the 12th local time, Huang Jing, chairman of the Moscow Overseas Chinese Federation, said excitedly when he saw the reporter of Sino-Singapore Network.
Not long ago, she participated in the "Overseas Chinese Cultural Society Chinese Talent (Calligraphy, Painting) Training Course" sponsored by the Overseas Chinese Affairs Office of the State Council of China and hosted by Jinan University.
When I just participated in the training course, I did not know where to start the calligraphy and painting, and at the end of the training course, you have been able to draw and write your own works.
After returning to Moscow, we must use the knowledge and skills you have learned to make your own contributions to the dissemination and promotion of Chinese culture.
At the same time, the Secretary-General of the Russian Association for the Promotion of Chinese Culture, who participated in this training course, Na Yanwei, had the same feeling.
She said that she has made great progress with the help of teachers in training courses, and she has also felt the responsibility of being an “overseas communicator of Chinese culture”.
After returning to Russia, he said that after returning to Russia, he will continue to spread and promote traditional Chinese culture among Chinese people and Russians who love Chinese culture.
