Leyman will serve as an expert of Bundesliga Asian media partners to participate in a variety of local fan events.
According to reports, in the autumn of this year, Bundesliga ambassadors Leyman and Mateus will represent Bundesliga in Asia and the Americas to carry out legendary journeys, for the opening of the Bundesliga 2016/17.
The event will span two continents, covering four top cities, and they will work with fans everywhere to warm up for the new season.
The Bundesliga is known as one of Europe's top five leagues (the Premier League, La Liga, Serie A, Bundesliga, Ligue 1), and is the flagship event of the German sports community in the Kingdom of Football.
As one of the most powerful leagues in the world, the Bundesliga attracted about 13.3 million spectators to the stadium in the 2014-2015 season alone.
Bundesliga giants Bayern Munich, Dortmund and famous stars Thomas Müller, Rahm, Gotzer and others are well known in China.
In line with the previously launched Weibo, Youku and WeChat Chinese platforms in the Bundesliga, the Bundesliga hopes to provide Chinese fans with a broader and timely and convenient channel to obtain the latest news of the league.
The British team won the silver medal in the rugby rugby game, and Fiji won the gold medal.
In Thursday night’s seven-side rugby final, Britain failed to continue their previous stellar performance in front of Fiji, having been beaten 43-7 at Rio Theodoro Stadium.
The Fiji team won the gold medal with an impeccable performance in possession of the ball, steal, avoidance, cooperation, running and strength, which is also the country's first ever Olympic medal.
The silver medal is also a great consolation for the defeated British team, which won the British delegation's third silver medal on the same day. This was enough to make the British rugby team very proud: they defeated New Zealand, Argentina and South Africa all the way in the seven-a-side rugby game, which entered the Olympic Games for the first time.
Earlier in the day, the British team narrowly defeated South Africa 7-5, which may have affected their status in the final.
But in any case, the current Fiji team is good enough to beat a full-spirited 15-man team.
Tomorrow, at least one Englishman will wear a gold medal, which may be a consolation for the British team, but it's also probably not. The Englishman is Ben Ryan, the head coach of Fiji from Wimbledon, who has served as the head coach of the English team.
It’s not easy for the British team to achieve today’s results.
Eight years ago, under Ryan’s coach, they didn’t win at the Adelaide International Sevens rugby game.
And now they’re just one step away from the championship.
Although they have suffered huge blows, they have also made amazing progress.
Fiji's opening has an advantage, so that the British team has no strength.
For Tom Mitchell and his teammates, it's like crashing into a series of running buses. When Ausi Colinisso stormed the horns, the World Series championship team was already far ahead with a 5-0 run.
Only four minutes into the game, Jerry Tuhuai scored again on the right.
12 to 0, the British team barely hit the ball.
Mitchell’s strong interception left the giant’s Lyon Nacarava without a third scoring, but that simply slows down Fiji’s scoring speed.
In 7 minutes, Yassa Weilemaru touched the ground in the right corner. 17-0, the British team made it even worse.
Nacarava scored another point, and the first half of the game ... was one minute left.
Vatmo Lavover then broke through England’s defence and went straight to the scoring line.
At half-time, the score was already 29-0.
Fijians are as if they were born to play rugby with seven men, and the English team is still a fledgling team.
This is the case.
England made a huge change in the second half and hit the Fijian's line of defense for a full four minutes, which was already good in the first half. But then the Fijian team made a good match, with Joshua Tuesova scoring again.
Dan Norton created the opportunity to score for the British team, and he changed the score to 36 to 7 on the left corner, but the game was already under the control of the South China Sea island countries, and their fans sang loudly on the platform, waving flags and singing and dancing.
Fiji's excellent performance makes people have to clap their hands quickly.
Marta William stopped an inconceivable attack by Fiji in the last minute.
At the end of the whistle, the Fijians hugged together, and the defeated British team could only regret retiring.
Earlier in the day, Fiji defeated Japan 20-5 in the semi-finals, while the United Kingdom narrowly defeated South Africa in an intense semi-final showdown.
In the first half, Kyle Brown helped South Africa take the lead, but Dan Norton scored in the second half with an excellent footplay.
After that, England Anthony's brother, Marcus Watson, secured the team's victory with a wonderful interception, and in the end, England won the silver medal.
Helen Graff and Heather Stanning were inspired by a coach suffering from cancer and won the rowing gold medal.
It’s no exaggeration to say it’s one of the most exciting gold medals.
From the beginning of the first paddle to now, Helen Graff and Heather Stanning have received 220 punitive pull training, and the gold medal they won in Estacio da Lagoa is even more significant.
Although only two of them were paddled, there was also a person on the boat - coach Robin Williams - the voice has been accompanying them to impact the second consecutive women's sculls Olympic gold medal, which is Britain's first pair of rowing women's group to reach this height.
They have maintained an unbeaten record of 39 games, with an absolute advantage.
What we’ve seen is that these two talented athletes marched gracefully on the water, but that’s not the whole thing about winning.
There are many people who volunteer to help behind the gold medal of each rowing boat, and it is their continuous dedication that has created a difference, and the greatest help is a coach who learns 30 months ago that he is suffering from cancer and does not know whether he can live to see this day.
As he said, death can come at any time.
I had bladder cancer and they operated on me.
Without surgery, cancer cells will spread throughout the body.
In this way, the situation will be much worse.
This will slightly change your mind.
Williams was diagnosed with cancer in December 2013.
Fortunately, he started treatment in early 2014 and minimized the impact, although it may not be appropriate to say so in this case.
I have to get paid, so I have to get better quickly.
It’s an incentive for me.
I was in the hospital, and although they said a few steps was enough, I walked around the ward 20 feet, 30 feet, 50 feet each time around the ward.
That’s the starting point for everything.
Rowing itself is a journey, and it makes the journey a little bit longer.
The first thing that came to mind was Williams, at the moment of winning gold. This morning's Williams was a little more chatty than usual in order to overcome his anxiety.
Steining, who was the captain of the Royal Artillery team, will travel to Afghanistan, saying: "I'm in a very bad mood this week, it may be a bit extreme, but this gold medal is of great significance."
It repeatedly told me how important it was to me, how hard I, Helen and Robin worked.
It’s been three years for Helen, Robin, and I’ve worked hard in return.
“Without Robin, we’re just unknown, thank you very much, he’s the best coach in the world.”
I couldn’t have found a better trainer and coach than him.
Helen Graff and Heather Stanning did not fail in five years.
The penalties set by this combination are incomparable to those imposed by their opponents.
Even in the final 500 meters, New Zealand and Denmark began to approach, Stanning and Graff still had a lot of physical reserves.
It was amazing at the time.
Helen said, “Keep up the rhythm, keep the pace.”
It is very important not to be influenced by the opponent.
We had a good start, and we weren’t looking forward to anything earth-shattering.
“We didn’t think about today’s glory, we just wanted to draw every paddle and win the game, and we did it.
It took the group a year to decide their future.
Graff will be married next month to television explorer Steve Buckshall.
But for now, she just wants to enjoy the moment.
I don't want to say it's my last game.
This will put too much pressure on me.
In London, it took me about six months to realize that I was an Olympic champion.
It’s a completely new experience, and I’m very nervous.
It’s been about 4 minutes now.
She said, "I'm feeling better."
The stunning structure of the Los Angeles Central Library
The Southern California chapter of the American Society of Architectural Historiologists and the authors of the new book, The Central Museum of Los Angeles: The History of Art and Architecture, Arnold Swatzmann and Steven Gee, held a salon. Visitors can learn more about the history of the downtown central library through this event.
Gee and ŠŠłazmann will discuss and share images of the 1926 design of Betlen Goodsey as well as the restoration and expansion of Hardy Holzmann Fufl in 1933.
Salon time: August 21 from 2 p.m. to 4 p.m. at Salle Moderne, Art Deco Southwestern School of Law (formerly Bullocks Wilshire), 3050 Wilshire Blvd.
Participants can visit the Central Hall, the Times Room, the Cactus Lounge and the Tea Room.
Pre-reservation required; SAHSCC members: $15; Non-members: $25.
DTLA's open factory loft underwent a cosy renovation.
Celebrating the 90th anniversary of the Los Angeles Central Library and the sale of new books
For the first time in eight months, Bulgaria has experienced inflation.
According to national statistics, the monthly inflation rate in Bulgaria was 1% in July.
This is the highest rate of inflation in several years (since June 2012). After October last year (inflation of 0.2%), it exceeded zero for the first time.
Compared with the previous 12 months (August 2014 to July 2015), the average annual inflation rate (measured by the consumer price index) for the past 12 months (August 2015 to July 2016) was -0.8%.
Compared with June 2016, the consumer price index in July 2016 was 101.0%, that is, the monthly inflation rate was 1.0%.
The inflation rate so far this year (July 2016 relative to December 2015) is -0.2%. Compared with July 2015, the annual inflation rate in July 2016 was -0.2%.
Compared with the previous month, the prices of the following categories of consumer goods increased in July 2016: food and non-alcoholic beverages (1.7%), transportation (1.8%), entertainment and culture (6.3%), restaurants and hotels (1.2%), and other goods and services (0.3%).
Prices fell in clothing and footwear (2.2%), furniture, home appliances and conventional maintenance (0.5%), and medical (0.1%).
Alcoholic beverages and tobacco, housing, water, electricity, natural gas and other fuels, communications, education, which were the same as last month's prices.
Snapchat’s ‘anime’ effect has been accused of satirizing Asians.
Snapchat says the filter was inspired by anime, but some observers believe it’s racist.
Snapchat’s 150 million daily users can change reality through its filtering tools and make portraits funny.
You can turn yourself into a pineapple, a dog, or a character in Roy Lichtenstein’s paintings.
These lenses have the effect of passivation and bending characteristics, resulting in more than 30 million modified selfies every day.
Any mistakes will immediately be noticed by the public.
Snapchat lenses have been criticized, and the app has been accused of agitating to play black people or to use white skins for beauty.
So, when the app this week provided some users with a filter that could create oblique eyes, weird teeth, and pink-face effects, some commentators referred to it as racial satire on Asian “yellow people.”
They even believe that whether these recurring questions means that the company has a big problem with diversity.
After Snapchat said it removed the feature, reports from The Verge and Motherboard on Wednesday sparked outrage.
The company’s explanation is that the filter is a tribute to the anime characters, rather than satirizing Asians.
But for observers who have experienced racism, the filter reminds them of harmful stereotypes in reality.
Others are also strongly opposed to these anime images.
One Korean-American art student, who tweeted about the photos and was widely shared, said in an email that the filters were “at least unpleasant and uncomfortable.”
“It’s very difficult to distinguish between the extremely disgusting Asian satirical images and the effects of the filters,” she said.
Although it is not only the yellow people in the filter, but the yellow people are extremely demeaning.
Snapchat isn’t the only company touching the bottom lines of these cultures.
From the company’s board to Hollywood and the devices we carry, American culture seems to have been advocating for diversity and inclusion.
Snapchat’s large group of young people may be very sensitive because they pay more attention to racial diversity than the older generation.
When one of Snapchat’s filters created an image that insulted users, 25-year-old Judith said in an interview on Thursday: “It’s harder to escape than before.”
On Thursday, Ms. Zhu, who worked as a product manager and engineer at Medium, decided to delete her Snapchat account and encourage others to do the same.
In an article written for Medium and in a phone interview, she said she believed the race controversy reflected Snapchat’s lack of racial diversity in hiring.
Ms. Zhu criticized the company’s employees for being mostly white, the leadership was all male, and at the end of the article added a hashtag: #Delete Snapchat.
As a Chinese-American, Ms. Zhu said, “Either their employees don’t have all kinds of people, so they can make such a decision, or there are people of color among their employees, but their positions don’t allow them to speak freely.”
Other observers shared complaints that she did not respond to by Snapchat.
The company did not release data on the diversity of its employees and said it was a private company.
On Thursday, Snapchat declined to discuss the racial context of its employees, but a spokesperson said the company recently hired a recruiter to focus on a lower percentage of people internally and to promote internal inclusion.
Ms. Zhu said she would shut down her Snapchat account: “I wonder if they need more users like us who oppose this behavior.”
The congressional panel said military officials had distorted ISIS intelligence.
According to a report released by a congressional panel on Thursday, U.S. Central Command officials changed their intelligence reports to describe the fight against ISIS in Iraq and Syria more optimistic than they really are.
This interim report comes from a special working group formed by the Republican chairman of the House Armed Services Committee, the Intelligence Committee, and the House Appropriations Committee's defense subcommittee. The report said there were "widespread grievances" among Central Command intelligence analysts, who said their superiors were tampering with their assessments of the U.S.-ISIS war.
Central Command (Centcom) in Tampa, Florida is the military headquarters responsible for overseeing U.S. military operations in the Middle East and Central Asia.
According to a news story about the report, “intelligence reviewed by the senior leaders of Central Command is more optimistic about U.S. counter-terrorism operations than it really is, and has always been more optimistic than the analysis of other intelligence agencies.”
“Central Command’s actions are unacceptable. On the one hand, our warriors are suffering from war, and on the other, top policymakers receive the wrong analysis.”
Central Command’s leadership issues have been extended to the highest levels of the agency.
The report details the long-standing problems of Central Command in 2014 and 2015 in describing and analyzing U.S. training for Iraqi troops.
While there is no definitive evidence that senior Obama administration officials ordered these reports to be changed, according to the report’s descriptions, these analysts felt themselves under pressure from Central Command leaders to express more optimism about threats from ISIS or ISIL.
“In the first half of 2015, many Central Command press releases, statements and congressional testimony were far more optimistic than they really were,” the report said.
For example, a Central Command official publicly stated that a major military operation to retake Mosul as early as April or May 2015.
Mosul, Iraq’s second-largest city, is still under Islamic State control.
Mike Pompeo, the Republican representative of Kansas, said in a statement: "After several months of investigation, this result is very obvious."
From mid-2014 to mid-2015, most of U.S. Central Command’s top intelligence officials manipulated the Command’s intelligence products, concealing threats from the Islamic State of Iraq.
After the Republicans learned from the analysts that intelligence on the Islamic State had been manipulated, they set up a special working group.
As the investigation continues, there will be more findings after this report was released on Thursday.
The Attorney General of the Department of Defense also conducted a long-term investigation of the Central Command.
Democratic members of the House Intelligence Committee released their findings on Thursday, in line with some of the conclusions of the Republican Task Force.
In a statement, Mr. Xie, the committee’s Democratic leader’s representative, said in a statement that between 2014 and 2015, Central Command’s intelligence assessments of Islamic State and Iraqi peacekeeping forces developed an overly narrow process.
Mr. Xie Anda said the process “obstructed the release of intelligence”, reduced the morale of analysts and “cannot accept different views”.
But Mr. Sheranda and Democrats also said they had found no evidence that the White House was trying to put pressure on Central Command analysts, so that their conclusions were in line with “presuppositions or political narratives.”
On Tuesday, the Daily Beast reported the preliminary results of a congressional investigation.
Last August, the New York Times reported that the Pentagon’s attorney general began an investigation after receiving complaints from Central Command analysts.
Pentagon spokesman Navy Major Patrick Evans said in a statement that the Department of Defense did not make any comments on this congressional report before the end of the attorney general’s investigation.
“Experts sometimes disagree on the interpretation of complex data, and intelligence agencies and the Department of Defense encourage healthy dialogue on these important national security topics,” he said.
The impact of the investigation goes beyond whether the U.S.-led bombing campaigns in Iraq and Syria have succeeded (as increasingly claimed by defense officials).
Last year, however, those claims raised questions about the extent to which President Obama could trust Central Command’s assessment of military operations in Iraq, Afghanistan, Libya, and other crisis areas.
Criticism of Islamic State intelligence is reminiscent of controversy more than a decade ago, when Central Command intelligence analyst Gregory Hook wrote a research article in which George W. Bush's administration, despite the opposition of many analysts, insisted on sending small-scale troops to Iraq and gave little consideration to what happened after the 2003 invasion.
Mr. Hook played a key role in this campaign against Islamic State intelligence.
Last year, officials said Mr. Hooke’s team’s findings that airstrikes against Islamic State refineries did not significantly reduce the terrorist group’s economic income, as the group’s construction of temporary refineries to continue selling oil on the black market was very much different from the announcement.
According to Time magazine's September report, Central Command did not release the discovery.
When multiple lawyers reviewed Senate testimony about an overly optimistic assessment of the war, Central Command commander Lloyd Austen III was criticized last year.
General Austin retired in April and is currently being replaced by Joseph Wotl in his position at Central Command.
The U.S. has won the women’s Hockey Tournament by four in a row and will win against Britain.
Katie Bam, who was tied in a 6-1 win over Japan, took the lead for the U.S. women’s hockey team twice on Thursday, helping the U.S. beat India 3-0.
Five goals in two games were four, but the 27-year-old said she didn’t know she had done so well.
She said, "I don't know anything about it."
“I’m not the kind of person who remembers that I’ve scored a few goals.
What she knows is that the U.S. team has won four straight at the Olympics and will compete with the team in the group for the No. 1 in the British team who did not lose after Thursday’s 2-0 victory over Japan.
Britain and the United States met narrowly in the final game of Saturday's first round.
Both teams advanced to the quarter-finals, and the match will determine who will appear as the first in the group.
The team that finished first in the group will avoid encountering a strong Dutch team, thus being able to go much further. The Netherlands came out as first in the other group.
During Saturday's competition, the U.S. team performed a miracle with an amazing performance. At the London Olympics four years ago, the U.S. team was at the bottom of 12 teams.
Bam was also on that team at the time.
Bam, who grew up in Brubel, Pennsylvania, first picked up a hockey stick at the age of three (her twin sister was in the sport at Drexel) and joined the national team at the age of 16, becoming the youngest member of the national team to date.
She missed out on the 2008 Olympics because she failed to make the final list.
In 2012, neither she nor her teammates were watchful.
The following year, Englishman Craig Panam was the manager, and everything began to change.
“This is a change of culture, mentality and substance.”
At the time, we were not at our current level in London.
We came here with a complete turnaround.
On Thursday night, Bam took the lead in the first half with a close-range back-hand shot.
India's victory has not yet tasted in this competition, but this team has shown amazing tenacity and kept the score of 1-0 until the end of the third quarter, when Bam broke out.
She took the ball along the left side of the course long-distance attack, and then cut inside to the middle of the road, drawn into the net, the U.S. team took a 2-0 lead.
Melissa Gonzales scored the final goal in the middle of the fourth quarter.
U.S. goalkeeper Jackie Briggis scored one goal each in the top three wins.
This time, she played very often.
Bam as well.
"We've been in good shape right now," Panam said. But exactly how good it is depends on the outcome of Saturday's game.
Shabby food during the Great Depression.
In March 1933, Franklin Delano Roosevelt, who had just been elected president, was sitting in the president’s office for lunch.
As a foodie, President Roosevelt liked the cuisine of Fifth Avenue, such as foie gras and Maryland stew.
On that day, his menu was very simple: ketchup for the devil's eggs, mashed potatoes, and fruit pudding as a snack.
Jane Ziegman said, “This is to share in food with those who are suffering.”
Her husband, Andrew Key, added: "This also reflects the way Americans eat."
The couple living in Brooklyn Heights are food historians.
In Mr. Koe’s last book, “Frying Scorched Vegetables,” was about Chinese food in the United States, and Ms. Ziegman told the story of the lives of tenants in the ghetto through food in her book 97 Orchard.
Their co-wrotted new book, The Plenty Meal, will be published Tuesday by Harper’s Press, an introduction to America’s food history during the Great Depression.
After presenting some common insights in terms of food, they met a reporter at a sandwich shop in Eisenberg. This simple lunch counter in the iron zone has been in business since 1929, when the economy collapsed.
The 54-year-old Ms. Zigman ordered a cream cheese with a broken olive sandwich, while 57-year-old Mr. Ko ordered turkey, mashed potatoes and vegetable platters.
The reporter ordered a baked meat roll, and the couple decided that these dishes were suitable for discussing the diet during the Great Depression.
Ms. Ziegman said, “Bread was very popular at the time.”
At that time, there was peanut bread, liver bread, and soy bread.
They are all made with a raw material and a kind of cheap tow that can be poured on raw materials.
Imagine that your dinner is full of peanuts.
Mr. Ke was making a strange appearance. 🙂
He said, "They're like lead in your stomach."
In the years leading up to the Great Depression, the Americans had a buffet, especially in the suburbs.
A group of women cooked meals for male farm workers, and there were just-examined pies for breakfast, lunch and dinner.
During World War I, it was the Americans who gave food to hungry Europeans. The Plenty Meal chronicled how the country suddenly ceased to be a place of abundance.
He explained why he and his wife wrote the book: “At that time, food had become a major topic of displeasure for Americans.”
Another unpleasant topic is shabby new foods: “fascinations” such as bread and stew have become the main dish, and stew is “the best way to cook leftovers,” Ms. Ziegman said, because chefs can use the cream in the sauce to cover up hard-to-eat ingredients.
Fresh fruits are substituted with cheap dried fruits.
The flesh that has been taking the lead at the American table for many years has become a rarity of luxuries.
The strange hodgepod only considers calories, compared to taste, and even basic common sense of cooking, the first thing people think about is nutrition.
Over the course of researching this book, including various recipes, Ms. Ziegman produced a roasted onion stuffed with peanut oil.
"It's not common at the dinner table," Mr. Ko said. "It's not common at dinner tables."
Ms Ziegman said: “It’s also very strange.”
Peanut oil and roasted onions can not be matched.
This is characteristic of many family economic meals.
Family economists have influenced the country’s eating habits, such as Louis Stanley, who served as head chef of the Federal Bureau of Family Economics from 1923 to 1943.
They publish recipes and articles in newspapers and magazines, encouraging women to be “calculous” and have the courage to turn poor foods such as cream pasta with carrots into food.
"Plentiful Meal" is a rich "historical treasure".
It’s especially interesting to see the government’s responses to hungry people, such as Herbert Hoover, the president’s citizen’s “I can’t control other people’s things.”
Although he publicly praised the simple Iowa farmhouse in his childhood, his diet was as delicate as a millionaire.
He said: “He likes to eat European-style Western meals, such as fish with cucumber sauce.”
He wears an evening dress and eats in a gilded restaurant.
He was clearly out of the people.
Had it not been for wife Eleanor encouraging him to set an example in his diet, President Roosevelt would probably have made the same mistake.
As stated in this book, Ms. Roosevelt’s hired housekeeper has no interest in taste, so “food in the White House is not only the hardest food to eat in Washington, but also the worst in cooking.”
As soon as the U.S. returned to regularity, many Great Depression-era cooking methods were abandoned.
Ms. Zigman said what was left was our focus on calories and nutrition and the application of science to cooking.
The couple said that when they wrote this book, they learned more about the eating habits of Ms. Ziegman’s mother, such as how she didn’t discard the food.
He said, “She’s very afraid of wasting food.”
Ms. Ziegman recalled: “She had actually made many lives sick.”
For example, there has ever been a "cream puff" incident.
After removing the plate, she and Mr. Ko took out a dessert they had prepared at home: this was what President Roosevelt ate at lunch.
Ms. Ziegman said: "This is called the cream fruit", and added that the name of a new wave for an ordinary dish is "the usual trick".
There is no cream in this dessert, only fruit, a little flour, sugar, water and cinnamon.
It is difficult for everyone to find it difficult for them to rely into the sticky brown paste.
Unsurprisingly, this dessert tastes good.
Mr. Ke ate the second and third spoons again.
He felt that it was an acceptable and affordable dessert, so he told his wife, "Add a little broken walnuts to eat."
Unfortunately, OPEC's latest monthly report shows that crude oil production continued to increase in July, and Saudi Arabia's production reached a new high.
This report does not ban the market has cast doubt on OPEC's credibility, and the road to recovery in oil prices may still be full of thorns.
On Monday, OPEC’s rotating chairman and Qatar’s energy minister said that OPEC will hold an informal meeting on the sidelines of the International Energy Forum on September 26-28.
OPEC's monthly report on Wednesday showed that the entire Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC), including Gabon, rose by 46,000 bpd in July to 33.11 million bpd.
OPEC also said in its monthly report that the low price of crude has prompted global refiners to produce more refined oil products, thus increasing the degree of oversupply in the market.
Affected by this news, coupled with the increase in U.S. crude oil production expectations and an unexpected increase in crude oil inventories, international oil prices fell for two consecutive days.
As of Wednesday's close, light crude oil futures delivered on the New York Mercantile Exchange in September fell 2.48 per cent and London Brent futures delivered in October fell 2.07 per cent.
Reuters believes that the proposed meeting of oil producers is unlikely to significantly tighten supply, and the data released by the US Energy Information Administration has also suppressed the popularity of the market.
Iran's official news agency, Fars, quoted Iranian oil minister Zangane as saying on Wednesday that Iran's daily crude oil production was 3.85 million barrels, the highest level since 2008.
As soon as the news of the meeting, Russian Energy Minister Novak said that there is no need for a new round of frozen production negotiations under current oil prices.
The last meeting was in April, and OPEC members failed to reach an agreement on any measures.
Emma Richards, an oil and gas analyst at BMI Research, said markets and the media could overreact to OPEC’s upcoming meetings.
Helima Croft, head of commodity strategy at the Royal Bank of Canada, said OPEC had changed market sentiment by sending signals that they would facilitate the deal.
This method is like the smoke and the mirror that opens people's eyes (deliberately giving the wrong impression).
Eugen Weinberg, head of commodity research at Commerzbank, said the possibility of OPEC trying to stabilize the market at the September meeting was low.
This is likely to further undermine the market's confidence in OPEC, after all, this group staged a "wolf."
All localities should focus on spot checks on medical institutions that have illegally issued medical advertisements, concentrated complaints and reports, and have been punished many times before.
The National Health and Family Planning Commission and the State Administration of Traditional Chinese Medicine will organize and supervise the implementation of special supervision and inspection work in some provinces in a timely manner.
According to media disclosures, due to the large-scale influx of capital into Internet medicine, resulting in serious problems of homogenization of current products, the investment boom has gradually retreated, and capital has entered a wait-and-see period.
In addition, according to the data of Hong Kong's Alipi hospital management research center, the Internet medical company died a large number within one year, and about 20% of the start-up Internet medical enterprises have ceased to exist.
However, just as the majority of Internet medical enterprises are struggling on the financing path of Series A or Series B, there are still several leading companies in the subdivision that can still gain popularity with capital.
It seems that the Internet medical entrepreneurship can not be "a swarm", but to look at the market demand, sink down to be dedicated, do deep.
Yu Yue invested 12.00.00 million yuan, accounting for 40% of the registered capital, Kyushu Tong equipment company invested 18.00.00 million yuan, accounting for 60% of the registered capital.
In recent years, with the country's policy support for medical informatization, electronic and integrated supply chain management systems have gradually entered hospitals at all levels.
The cooperation between Yu Yue and Kyushu Tong is aimed at the needs of the market, helping hospitals to build an advanced supply chain management system, and seeking more cooperation as an opportunity.
Unlike many Internet medical companies, iBaby has focused on the vertical field of Internet obstetrics from the very beginning, deeply cultivating both pregnant mothers and doctors.
The pregnant mother can not only be free 24 hours and one-on-on-one doctor consultation, but also pay for targeted medical consultations.
At the doctor's side, iBaby breaks down geographical restrictions by organizing experts to give grass-roots doctors online lectures, peer exchanges, and case discussions.
At present, there are three sections on the doctor's side, namely, the doctor's continuing education, the doctor's society, and the doctor's help.
Provision includes online learning, case discussions, academic exchanges; social platforms with hospitals and doctors in the same department; legal assistance, entrepreneurial support and other services required for doctor-patient relationships or personal lives.
According to media reports, CEO Wang Lei recently said that Ali Health is "willing to sink his heart" to win health big data.
The lack of professionalism of Internet companies and data companies does not achieve uniformity in writing methods on the same terms.
Ali's current layout in the field of medical and health is divided into three pieces, which are Ali Health, Tmall Medical Museum and Alipay Future Hospital.
Wang Lei frankly said that medical health entrepreneurship will be more difficult than other industries, "this is not just a matter of how much money, but also to calm down, endure loneliness and do it slowly."
It is easy to damage the heart by staying up late to watch the Olympic Games.
Brazil's Olympic Games are in full swing, and even if the event is broadcast in the middle of the night in China, many citizens will stay up late to watch.
In this regard, the doctor specially reminded that there are hidden health risks in staying up late to see the event, which may cause cardiovascular diseases.
If you stay up late for a long time, the hormone will still secrete a lot, the human body will continue to be in a state of nervous excitement, unable to obtain normal recovery, easy to cause vasodilation, increased blood pressure, resulting in cardiovascular disease.
In particular, Han Zhiyuan reminded that groups with cardiovascular risk factors such as high blood pressure, high blood sugar, high blood lipids, smoking habits, family history and other cardiovascular risk factors will be more likely to cause cardiovascular disease if they stay up late.
If you stay up late for a long time, not only the cardiovascular function will be affected, but also the gastrointestinal function, the immune system, and the neuroendocrine system will be affected, and even the risk of tumors will increase.
For elderly friends, Han Zhiyuan recommends trying not to stay up late in order to watch the Olympic Games, especially groups with a history of cardiovascular diseases.
During the last "World Cup" football game, Han Zhiyuan had treated a patient in his 60s, and his myocardial infarction was triggered or related to staying up late to watch the game.
Han Zhiyuan introduced that since the beginning of this year, his department has received a number of patients around the age of 25 who have suffered from myocardial infarction or stroke, which is largely due to the patient's long-term stay-up lifestyle.
Don't stay up late every day, occasionally stay up late to watch your favorite sports, and other projects may wish to wait until the next day to watch the replay of the event.
When staying up late, add water and eat more fruits, which can prevent blocked blood vessels and enhance the body's immunity.
On August 12, Beijing time, the women's 50-meter rifle of the 2016 Rio Olympic Games won the final of the three postures, and Chinese veteran Du Li won the bronze medal.
Du Li has become an Olympic four-year veteran, winning a total of 2 gold, 1 silver and 1 bronze and four medals in the four Olympic Games.
In 1998, he entered the shooting team of Shandong Province and followed Coach Wang Devon for professional shooting training.
In June 2003, she participated in the Shooting World Cessation Women's 10m Air Rifle gold medal and broke the world record with 504.9 rings.
In August 2004, she won the gold medal in the women's 10m air rifle and won the first gold medal for the Chinese team at the Athens Olympic Games.
In August 2008, he won the gold medal with a total score of 690.3 rings to break the Olympic record in the 50-meter sports rifle.
In August 2012, after folding the London Olympic Games, Durie submitted a temporary retirement application to the FIA.
In January 20105, Douri announced that she would return to the national team to start training and prepare for the Rio Olympics.
In March 2016, the Rio Olympic trials ended, and after eight years, they once again qualified for the women's 10-meter air rifle Olympic Games.
On August 6, 2016, in the women's ten-meter air rifle competition at the Rio Olympic Games, Douli won the silver medal with 207 rings.
On August 12, 2016, he won the bronze medal in the women's 50-meter rifle three posture competition at the Rio Olympics.
The film is expected to premiere on CCTV and LeTV early next year, and will also launch a VR panoramic documentary for the first time.
The documentary "Polar" is a large-scale work focusing on the Qinghai-Tibet Plateau in the third pole of the earth, with a new perspective to tell the story of the intersection of Tibetan tradition and modernity and the interaction between Tibet and the world.
The biggest advantage of VR works is that the audience has a unique sense of "immersion", which also puts forward higher requirements for the filming process.
The filming team of the "Polar" Panorama VR Special Edition said that they want to ensure that the picture in every orientation is impeccable, so that the audience has an immersive feeling.
On August 11, the Yantai detachment of the Shandong Armed Police Corps organized special combat snipers to come to Kunyongshan to carry out jungle training in the high temperature of 34 degrees Celsius.
During the Cold War, the Soviet Union brought missiles into Cuba, which almost led to a nuclear war between the United States and the Soviet Union.
This incident is regarded as the peak of the Cold War, known as the "Cuban missile crisis."
However, what is little known is that, also during the Cold War, a powerful solar storm almost caused the United States to launch a nuclear war against the Soviet Union, and this event was not first announced by researchers until August 9.
On May 23, 1967, a powerful solar storm caused strong interference with U.S. military radar and radio communications in the Arctic.
These radars are part of the U.S. ballistic missile warning system and are used to monitor Soviet missiles.
The paper, completed by researchers at the University of Colorado, interviewed U.S. military personnel who were involved in forecasting and analyzing solar activities at the time, and consulted non-confidential literature.
In the 1960s, in order to prevent the Soviet Union's sudden nuclear war, the U.S. Air Force always had some warplanes carrying nuclear warheads flying into the sky.
U.S. military commanders did not know that the main culprit in this disturbance was the solar storm, not the Soviet Union, so they ordered the aircraft to be put into combat readiness.
Fortunately, the U.S. military’s solar activity since the late 1950s and its research into Earth’s electromagnetic jamming have finally prevented this potential military conflict.
Later, he summarized the information provided by the U.S. Air Force Aviation Weather Service and submitted a detailed report.
As a direct result of this solar storm, the U.S. military has since identified space weather as an operational concern and established a more robust space weather forecasting system.
In the daily travel of the public, found that the car was obstructed by unfamiliar vehicles, and in the absence of contact with the driver of unfamiliar vehicles, they could use the "WeChat removal" function to solve this problem.
Since August 11th, Xi'an traffic police WeChat service number "Xi'an traffic police" has launched a "WeChat car removal" service.
After the launch of this service, in daily life, when unfamiliar vehicles hinder their own vehicles when the driver is not on the spot, they can solve such problems through the use of the "WeChat mobile car" function.
The first function of this new service is fast and saves administrative costs; the other is to respect and protect the privacy of citizens; the third is all-weather and full-time services.
As long as the public has WeChat, it can be very convenient to operate on their own, which can be relatively convenient for both sides of the car transfer to "meet", alleviate the problem of parking difficulties, and reduce the occurrence of car-related public security cases.
On the other hand, for owners who refuse to move cars, illegally park or obstruct traffic, Xi'an traffic control department said that the traffic police will take different disposal measures according to the actual situation at that time, depending on the situation.
